-- A run of same-headed definitions that is not a clause group, with a
-- bracketed input in the third: the parser reports the error where it reports
-- it when it reads the run again from every definition, whether or not it
-- remembers the run (refutation of legalese/l4-ide#545's review, round 3;
-- jl4-test's "parser memo changes nothing" check covers this file).
f x MEANS 1
f x MEANS 2
f (x) MEANS 3
f x MEANS 4
g y MEANS 5
